NUM-18: take a full conduit's losses from its inflow (STEADY, KINWAVE)

When the inflow to a conduit exceeds its full flow, the steady-flow solve
in Routing.cpp and the kinematic-wave solve in KinematicWave.cpp cap the
inflow taken from the upstream node at the full flow and deliver the full
flow at the outlet. The conduit's evaporation and seepage loss, already
stored for the mass balance, is then taken from neither, so it is booked
without being removed from the water. Cap the inflow at the full flow plus
the loss instead, as the 5.3.0 patch does. Results do not change for
conduits without losses or that are not full.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-18_swmm600.patch

